From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ImpulseROM <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Synchronize screen resolution switching with display density

Stock S24 FE One UI 8.5 replaced setSelectedScreenResolution() with setDisplayMode()
which calls clearForcedDisplaySize() and relies on Display.setUserPreferredDisplayMode().
On legacy devices with a fixed-resolution physical panel (like d2x / Note10+), that mode
is unsupported by kernel/HWC and fails, leaving resolution and DPI desynchronized and
causing UI scaling breakage until screen zoom is toggled.

Backport legacy dynamic resolution control to calculate convertRatio and atomically apply
both forced display size and proportional density via WindowManager.setForcedDisplaySizeDensity().
